JoinNextLine doesn't update cursor position correctly

#### Description

The `JoinNextLine` method is not properly handling cursor position after joining lines. When joining two lines with a separator, the cursor position should be updated to reflect the new text structure, but it appears to remain at the original position.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```go
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/c-bata/go-prompt"
)

func main() {
    // Create a buffer with multiple lines
    buffer := prompt.NewBuffer()
    buffer.InsertText("line1\nline2\nline3", false, true)

    // Move cursor to first line
    buffer.CursorUp(2)

    // Join next line with a space separator
    buffer.JoinNextLine(" ")

    // Expected: "line1 line2\nline3"
    // Actual: cursor position and text don't match expected behavior
    fmt.Println("Buffer text:", buffer.Text())
    fmt.Println("Document lines:", buffer.Document().Lines())
}
```

The issue occurs when trying to join lines - the cursor position and text manipulation don't work as expected, particularly when there are multiple lines in the buffer.

